Word audio (the .mp3 files in this folder)

The recordings were made by a program (Piper, https://github.com/rhasspy/piper and its successor https://github.com/OHF-Voice/piper1-gpl)
with the voice "Amy" (en_US-amy-medium), then trimmed, level-adjusted, slightly sped up and converted to MP3 by the game's author.

The voice was fine-tuned from the Hi-Fi TTS voice of reader 92 (Cori Samuel; dataset by NVIDIA: Evelina Bakhturina, Vitaly Lavrukhin,
Boris Ginsburg and Yang Zhang; https://www.openslr.org/109/). That dataset: CC BY 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/).

The voice's model card (a copy is in MODEL_CARD_en_US-amy-medium.txt) names https://github.com/MycroftAI/mimic3-voices as its dataset, a repository
under CC BY-SA 4.0. That repository does not list an Amy voice, and the licence of Amy's original recordings is not documented; the Piper
project lists the voice among those without a documented licence.

As a precaution, these audio files are shared under CC BY-SA 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/).

The audio is provided as it is, without warranty of any kind.
This does not mean that the creators of the dataset or the voice approve of this game.
